The following post typifies a dangerous trend that is developing in
right-wing circles.  There has always been a paramilitary faction, but it
is now mushrooming far beyond in normal ultra-racist, knuckle dragging
circles into more mainstream, normally law abiding 
conservative-libertarian-constitutionalist circles. 

People seem to be forgetting enmasse that war for the future is mainly a
battle of ideas and are reaching for their guns in response to the
leftward impulse of the Clinton Administration.  All this can only justify
and therefore lead to tyranny as there is no mass support for armed,
conservtive militias. 

Apparently, this fad was started by an call by one Linda Thompson, an 
investigator the WACO mess, who called for an armed march on Washington 
to arrest the traitors in office.

In my book, Linda Thompson is suspect as an agent provacateur. 

---------- Forwarded message ----------
Date: Wed, 07 Sep 1994 12:37:00 -0600 (MDT)
From: FIREWALKER <CRITESLE@uvmain.uvsc.edu>
To: act@zilker.net

Subject: Re: FROM THE LISTOWNER (ACT)


I have noticed something very striking, and wanted to say something about it. 
This message seemed to be about the most appropriate one to do it on that I
have read so far, so here goes...

>We have had many new people join ACT in the last few weeks.  Perhaps
>this is due to the way that the Feds seem to be getting more and more
>out of control lately.  It is also partly due to the feelers that have
>been placed in several usenet newsgroups.

ACT is about the smallest list that I belong to in terms of membership.  We are
a good group of people with, I believe, good ideas on what is happening, etc. 
However, because of our size, we also see a relatively small part of what is
happening out there in net-land.  This is <NOT> a slam on ACT -- far from it. 
We are also not as affected by the high noise-to-info ratio that some of the
other lists (and newsgroups) are suffering through, or should I say being
bogged down with.  There are good people talking about important issues here. 
It is also about the only political form that I post to (the only other being
MORONI).

However, I do monitor several other politically oriented groups (I'd rather not
list them) that have quite a bit more members and perhaps cover totally
different subjects.  These range from libertarians (the Utah libertarian list
alone dwarfs ours) to socialists to some other patriot groups.  I try to read
the newsgroups, but the only newsfeed program that I have easy access to
crashes so often that I can barely keep up with that.

I am not saying these things to brag.  Not in the least.  I am saying them so
that you can understand that I am speaking from a perspective that is wider
than our group.  (this message is something that Lance could probably attest to
just as well)

Also, and the biggest part of why I am saying this is, I have been quite
inactive in the lists for the past while.  Due to computer problems and
business requirements, I went 23 days without checking my mail even once.  When
I got back, I had nearly 1,300 messages waiting!  I, of necessity, went through
them very quickly -- sometimes only getting a feel for what was being talked
about as opposed to actual content.  After a short time I was off again for
nearly three weeks.  I got back to another 1,200+ messages the day that Lance
asked if anyone knew where I was.  Again I went through them in quasi-scan
mode.  Today is the first day that I have been back since then, only 10 days in
this gap, and I have over 1,500 messages!  This one (the one that I am
responding to) was in the high 300's.

I have seen some real trends here.  Not just in ACT, but in all of them.

During the first three-week gap the Brady bill passed, the Waco trials were
coming to an end, etc.  During the second three-week gap we saw the crime bill
pass, Linda Thompson's explaination of her call to arms (which I have to say
really shook up the ant-farm!), etc.

So much for historical perspective.  Here is my main observation....

At one time, speaking basically of the time before these gaps in my activity,
people would talk about arming themselves for an open conflict with the
government in only hushed tones, so to speak.  There were things said, but only
in enuendo or third-person type of ways.  "...I know of someone who said that
if things kept going the way they were that perhaps sometime in the future they
might think about what it would take to perhaps start preparing themselves for
some kind of situation where anarchy or rioting might happen someplace around
where they might be at that time..."  You knew what they were really trying to
say, because you probably felt the same way yourself, but nobody, and I mean
<NOBODY>, in their right mind came right out and said it!

It is true that every once in a while someone would come right out and say
something like "...I'm going to bury my weapons until I need them against
<fill-in-with-your-least-favorite-government-organization>...", but they were
really fairly few and far between.  Mostly there were open discussions of what
the government is doing TO US, and how we can <legally> protect ourselves, etc.

What I saw after the first gap was a slightly more than subtle shift towards
people starting to take some kind of militant stand.  Things like "...I am not
going to stand for this any longer..." and "...we <must> start to prepare
because it is so far out of control that it will not recover..." might sum up
that period.

After the second gap, things were quite different.  I actually saw messages
from people who were forming (or had already formed) private militia
organizations who were seeking new members.  I read plans, strategies, times,
etc.  It is true that there was one that was a rather comical thread that I
believe was pointed towards His Magesty the Rush-less of Limbaugh, but that
was, if I am not mistaken, a parity taken from another group that was serious.

Now I am going through the 1,500 messages from this last week and a half, and
have already seen some things that exceed most of the messages that I saw
previously!  I can only wonder what the other 1,100+ contain...

Are these people the fringe fanatics that are trying to make fools out of the
patriot movements?  I honestly can't tell from this perspective.  However,
there <IS> one thing that is quite clear to me -- people are reaching the end
of their tolerance!

I remember when we first heard of Linda Thompson and her plan to attack D.C.,
en masse.  It sure looked like it was somewhat premature.  Our friend John
jumped right up and started a crusade against it.  Of course, in hind-sight, we
see what her plans were.  At the time, though, it just appeared that this was a
tremendously stupid move, and people like John were jumping all over it because
of that.  This is no slam on John -- I'm using this as an example of what
people were doing all over.  It seemed premature, and everyone knew it -- and
then reacted accordingly.

But I am not seeing this kind of reaction now.  In fact, I haven't seen <any>
negative reaction to these more militant, more open, more agressive messages. 
It seems to me to be quite the opposite.  Thus a shift not only in the things
that are being said, but in the way that people are feeling about what is being
said as well.

When I gave my keynote address, I identified what I saw as the four phases or
stages in the revolutionary war, and tried to put them into today's patriot
movement perspective.  To summarize, these four phases were: 1) getting
information out to the people, 2) using any and all legal means to make changes
within the system, 3) civil disobedience, non-violent types for as long as
physically possible, and 4) all out war.

It was my assessment that the patriot movement had been stuck in phase one for
so long that anyone trying to move on to phase two or three was somehow seen as
doing something 'wrong.'  I called for all patriot organizations to basically
cease phase one activities whenever possible, and move forward, using their
personal vision as the only real guide.

We are at war, I said, and still say.  This is a real, honest to goodness,
people getting killed, war.  It's time that we started acting like it.  I
cannot in my wildest dreams imagine that my 'call to arms' has had any impact
on what I am seeing across the internet and bbs's, though.  (I'm not <that>
conceited...)  What I think is happening is that this message has become
obvious to everyone in their own right.

Whatever hot-button that they had; whatever vision that they were holding on
to; whatever invisible line that they had drawn in their minds past which they
would not allow the government to intrude; whatever their pet 'right' was that
could not be violated or threatened; where ever they were watching for some
violation that would stand as their bellweather of things to come -- no matter
what it is, it appears to me that Komrad Klinton and krew has succeeded in
smashing right through it!

It appears to me that the sheeple are starting to really wake up!  They are
waking up, and are mad as hell.  If this continues at the rate that I am
seeing, we could be seeing an armed conflict before Thanksgiving! (instead of
"...eat your turkey..." it could be "...eat this, turkey!!!")

I both look forward to that day and greatly fear it.  May God bless us that our
fight is righteous; that we are on His side!  And grant us the strength to be
victorious.

Lee


